A void atlas is a book of maps for travel along the [[Phenomena/Infinite Horizon|Horizon]]. Its first page is a fold-out chart of the voidward worlds, unfolding again and again to a length of about two hundred feet and covering close to two and a half million worlds. Somewhere a matching star atlas charts the other direction. The writing on the chart shifts as it is read, the words seeming to be rewritten over themselves, and the parchment is worn from the hands that used it before.

The Party's copy came from [[Org/The Harlequins/People/Ocelith|Ocelith]]'s library in [[Org/The Harlequins/Harlequin Town|Harlequin Town]], signed out with a name and the date on a card in the front cover. The last entry on the card was six months old, in the hand of [[People/Alastair Moss|Alastair Moss]], who works on the [[Org/Embercall Industries/index|Embercall]]'s research into the [[Voidsong]].

The worlds charted nearest the [[Org/The Harlequins/Providence|Providence]] include [[Geography/Menagerie|Menagerie 1]], a city that moves, and two Joker spans that run side by side, [[Geography/Hellsmith|Hellsmith]] and [[Geography/Glacier|Glacier]].
